  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Climate Efficient Services in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine&apos;s transition to low carbon emission services and energy efficient infrastructures has been severely impacted by the 2022 full-scale invasion by Russia and continuing war. Before the war, 10 million people across the country lacked access to safely managed water services, with approximately 20 million people unable to access centralized wastewater collection and treatment services. Widespread shelling through late 2022 has dramatically worsened access to vital utility services dependent on electricity. Rising energy costs have highlighted the importance of modernizing Ukraine&apos;s infrastructure and accomplishing with carbon dioxide emission reduction goals. 
 
With this contribution from the Government of France, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is responding to these issues through the restoration of water, sanitation and hygiene systems damaged by the war, by providing necessary repairs, replacements, and consumables and ultimately support safe and adequate access to water, sanitation, and heating services for conflict-affected populations. IOM is also improving access to renewable energy sources and climate efficient services through the upgrade of critical infrastructure. Additionally, the contribution is supporting research and data collection related to priority needs and population distribution across Ukraine to support evidence-based programming.</narrative>
  </description>
